67373	67473	67370	67371	the woman	1759	" that the Katherine Wilmot alluded to was perhaps no better than she should be , and had become more intimate with Mr. Tracy than my poor sister suspected . That , I thought , was the reason why she had poisoned my sister in order to get her out of the way , and for herself to remain at Mr. Tracy 's house . But I did not think that Mr. Tracy himself had any hand in the murder ; and so I did not see the good of producing a letter which would only expose Mr. Tracy . "
