71210	71430	71202	71202	Smithers	663	" I am no great hand at making speeches , sir ; but I ca n't take my leave of you , without saying something to convince you that I 'm not ungrateful for what you 've done for my niece . Your goodness , sir , has saved her from death ; and more than that , has proved her innocence . You are the best man I ever met in my life : you are more like an angel than a human being . I did n't think that such men as you could be in existence . It makes me have a better opinion of the world when I look upon you . How happy would a country be if it had such a person as yourself for its sovereign ! I can not understand my own feelings in your presence : I seem as if I could fall at your feet and worship you . Then I think that I am unworthy even to breathe the same air that you do . But your words have made me happy to some extent : for years I have not felt as I feel to - day . I can say no more , sir : I do n't know how I came to say so much ! "
