87062	87236	87060	87060	Aischa	650	" When he was so far recovered as to be able to speak — which was about half an hour after the blood was stanched — he implored me to have him removed from the Palace . He told me a long and pathetic story of persecutions and sufferings which he had undergone ; and he offered to enrich our treasury if we would take him beyond the reach of the person who had wounded him . His anxiety to get away was extreme ; and it was in consequence of his representations and promises that I prevailed upon the King to issue orders to those who were to leave London with us , to hurry the departure as much as possible . That accounts for the abrupt manner in which we left at such an hour , and for the removal of the wounded man with us . In answer to your direct question , I must inform you that he did _ not _ die of the wound which he received . "
87237	87245	87247	87247	Markham	612	" He did _ not _ die ! "
