119931	119935	119937	119937	Greenwood	604	" With pleasure , "
119977	119992	119994	119995	the nobleman	4032	" There is a constant supply of hot water , kept ready for use , "
119997	120097	119994	119995	the nobleman	4032	" Each room is provided with a marble bath ; and vases of eau - de - cologne afford the means of cooling the water and imparting to it a delicious perfume at the same time . You will also find wines , fruits , and all species of delicate refreshments there ; and adjoining each bath - room is a bed - chamber . With Malkhatoun as your companion , you may imagine yourself a Sultan in the privacy of his harem ; and , remember , that no soul will intrude upon you in that joyous retreat . "
120313	120320	120322	120322	Richard	612	" Yes , my adored one , "
120329	120380	120322	120322	Richard	612	" it is decided ! To - morrow I embark on this expedition . But I could not quit England without seeing you once more , dearest Isabella ; and for two or three days have I vainly wandered in this neighbourhood with the hope of meeting you — alone . "
120381	120405	120407	120408	the Princess	2663	" Oh ! Richard , had I for one moment divined that you were so near , I should have come to you , "
120410	120475	120407	120408	the Princess	2663	" and this you know well ! If I have hitherto discouraged clandestine meetings and secret correspondence — save on one or two occasions — it was simply because you should not have reason to think lightly of me;—but you are well aware , Richard , that my heart is thine — unchangeably thine,—and that my happiest moments are those I pass with thee ! "
120476	120500	120502	120502	Richard	612	" I can not chide you , dearest , for that fine feeling which has made you discourage clandestine meetings and secret correspondence , "
120517	120559	120502	120502	Richard	612	" but now that circumstances are about to change,—now that I shall be far away from thee , beloved girl,—that restriction must in some degree be removed , and you will permit me to write to you from time to time . "
120560	120578	120580	120580	Isabella	606	" It would be an absurd affectation and a ridiculous prudery , were I to refuse you , "
120582	120594	120595	120595	she	606	" Yes , dear Richard — write to me;—and write often , "
120604	120793	120795	120795	Richard	612	" A thousand thanks , Isabella , for this kind permission — this proof of your love . And , oh ! to whatever perils I am about to oppose myself face to face,—in whatever dangers I may be involved,—whatever miseries or privations I may be destined to endure,—the thought of you , my own adored Isabella , will make all seem light ! But I do not anticipate much difficulty in the attainment of our grand object . General Grachia , Colonel Morosino , and the other chiefs of this enterprise , have so well , so prudently , so cautiously digested all the measures necessary to ensure success , that failure is scarcely possible . The tyranny of the Grand Duke and of his shameless Ministry has reduced the Castelcicalans to despair . We have three fine vessels ; and twelve hundred devoted patriots will form the expedition . The moment we land , we shall be welcomed with enthusiasm . And if an opportunity should serve for me to show myself worthy of the confidence that General Grachia and his colleagues have placed in me,—if , "
120865	120865	120853	120853	he	0	"
120866	120875	120877	120879	the Italian lady	4223	" Of that I feel convinced , Richard , "
120891	120961	120877	120879	the Italian lady	4223	" But you know not the wild hopes — the exalted visions which have at times filled my imagination , since I heard a few weeks ago that you were one of the chiefs of this enterprise , the preparations for which were communicated to my father . For you are doubtless aware that General Grachia _ has _ made my father acquainted with his intentions and projects — — "
120962	120968	120970	120970	Richard	612	" Which the Prince discountenances , "
120976	121018	120970	120970	Richard	612	" Nevertheless , he is perhaps right : but if we succeed , Isabella — oh ! if we succeed , your father becomes the sovereign of a great and enlightened people ! Then — what hope will remain for me ? "
121019	121028	121030	121030	Isabella	606	" Providence will not desert us , Richard , "
121032	121094	121030	121030	Isabella	606	" Said I not ere now that the wildest hopes — the most exalted visions have dazzled my imagination ? I will not describe them to you , Richard ; but need I confess that they are connected with yourself ? The dying words of our poor friend Mary Anne have made an impression upon me which I can never forget . "
121095	121116	121118	121118	Markham	612	" I can well divine all the hopes and aspirations which _ her _ prophetic language was calculated to excite , "
121120	121176	121118	121118	Markham	612	" for there have been moments when I was weak enough to yield to the same influence myself . But the future is with the Almighty ; and He must ordain our happiness or our misery ! I must now leave you , my beloved Isabella:—when I am away thou wilt think of me often ? "
121177	121199	121201	121201	Isabella	606	" Oh ! Richard , will you really depart ? will you venture on this expedition , so fraught with danger ? "
121217	121271	121201	121201	Isabella	606	" I told you to hope — I wished to console you ; but it is I who require consolation when about to say farewell to you ! Oh ! Richard , if you knew what anguish now fills my heart , you would be enabled to estimate all my love for you ! "
121272	121282	121284	121284	Markham	612	" I do — I do , adored Isabella ! "
121292	121419	121284	121284	Markham	612	" How devotedly — how faithfully you have loved me , I never can forget ! When spurned from your father 's house — overwhelmed with the most cruel suspicions , your love remained unchanged ; and in many a bitter , bitter hour , have I derived sweet solace from the conviction that thy heart was mine ! Oh ! Isabella , God in his mercy grant that I may return from this enterprise with some honour to myself ! It is not that I am influenced by motives of selfish ambition;—it is that I may remove at least one of the hundred obstacles which oppose our union . And now adieu , my angel — my dearly - beloved Isabella : adieu — adieu ! "
121420	121436	121438	121438	Isabella	606	" Farewell , Richard — farewell , dearest one — my first and only love , "
121485	121493	121495	121495	Richard	612	" Let us be firm , Isabella , "
121497	121513	121495	121495	Richard	612	" who can tell what happiness my share in this enterprise may create for us ? "
121514	121526	121528	121528	Isabella	606	" Yes — something tells me that it will be so , "
