336502	336682	336497	336497	he	612	" when we can escape from all the ceremony which accompanies rank and power , and indulge uninterruptedly in that discourse which is so dear to hearts that love like ours ! For I have so much to tell you , beloved one ; and now that all the perils of war and strife are past , I can look with calmness upon that series of events of which I was only enabled to send you such slight and rapid accounts . But , believe me , Isabella — I would much rather have come back to my native shores unattended by all that ostentation and formal observance which have accompanied my return : nevertheless , the high office with which I was invested , and the respect due to your father by the one who came to announce with befitting ceremony that a throne awaited him , demanded the presence of that state and required that public demonstration . You must not , however , imagine , dearest one , that a sudden elevation has made me vain . "
