478974	479143	479462	479464	THE OBSTINATE PATIENT	12648	" Faithful to the promise which I made to you the day before yesterday , my dear aunt , I have quitted the West End , and am once more located in a quiet neighbourhood . Thanks to the kind interference of that most amiable and excellent nobleman the Prince of Montoni , and to the encouragement given me by your forgiveness of the deception which I so shamefully practised upon you , I have been completely awakened to the errors of my late mode of life . I shall pledge myself to nothing now : my future conduct will prove to you how effectually wise counsels and past experience have changed my habits , my inclinations , and my ideas . One thing , however , I may state on the present occasion : namely , that I am convinced there is no character so truly dangerous and so thoroughly unprincipled as the one who delights in the name of ' _ the man about town _ . '
